        "Bilirubin: the lab orders the BI046 panel, so DBILC/TBILC target its parameters 430 (Conjugated) / 431 (Total). A standalone BI048 'Bilirubin Total' order is still filled by name (same testname), as are standalone BI019 Albumin / BI186 Total Protein via the name key.",
        "GLU and RF stay TEST-level (no paramId) so the AU variant resolver can fill whichever glucose / RA-factor variant the sample ordered.",
        "Applying this preset OVERWRITES the driver's rules for these codes. That is deliberate: on 2026-10-02 the Jammu preset was applied on this PC and left Jammu's rules on the shared beckman-au480 driver (e.g. TP -> BI183, a test-level BI046 Direct-bilirubin rule). Re-onboarding with this preset restores Haldwani's targets. Codes not listed (AMY, AMY06, LIPASE, PHOS, CRPHS, the BuBc bilirubin blanks, LIH) had no Haldwani writes and are left as they are."
